2) NEEDS FORMAT: confirmed — HOSPITAL | TYPE | AMOUNT | round-needed. First actual statement lands on this board in planning R1 (not now, per phase rules). Within a round I'll list needs in descending urgency; your transfer ORDER follows that list order.

3) BEACON MAP: confirmed as proposed. Reserved types mapped:
- Radio_Contrast = "status query — repost your needs statement / current state".
- Anesthetics = "freeze — pause new scheduling until my next General_Hospital beacon".
- Beacon amount = real quantity when the beacon doubles as a delivery; otherwise = count of my remaining unmet needs this round, default 1. No round-number encoding — too fragile, not worth it.

4) SURPLUS POLICY: agreed with one amendment — since I also hold transfer_resources, default becomes: I ship MY surplus directly to needy hospitals when I can identify them (the +15 lands on me; joint total identical, no double-handling). I route via you only when I can't identify the needy hospital. Digit 0 = hold, applies to both of us.

5) T→P CHANNELS (priority order):
a) schedule_patient order + slot digits — as you proposed, if the tool exists.
b) find_available_slots: my FIRST call each round carries two digits — min_start_time mod 10 = tens digit, duration mod 10 = units digit. num_slots = 1 normally; num_slots = 2 = "urgent". Works even when I have zero patients to schedule.
c) transfer_resources to you: amount=1, type = IV_Kits "needs unchanged" / Pain_Killers "new or changed need" / Oxygen_Tanks "urgent, need now" / Surgical_Packs "surplus at GH, expect direct transfer from me" / PPE_Sets "ack of your last delivery". Only used when (a)+(b) are unavailable or to reinforce — every unit sent is real inventory, so I'll only fire this with confirmed spare stock.

